@startuml sequence_auth_oauth_vk

title COOKie MVP - OAuth 2.0 Authentication Flow (VK ID)\nGET /api/v1/auth/oauth/vk

actor "User (Browser)" as User
participant "OAuthInitController" as InitController
participant "VK ID\nOAuth Server" as VKOAuth
participant "OAuthCallbackController" as CallbackController
participant "JWT Service" as JWT
database "PostgreSQL\nusers table" as DB

== OAuth Initiation Flow ==

User -> InitController: GET /api/v1/auth/oauth/vk

activate InitController

InitController -> InitController: Generate CSRF state token\nstate = random_string(32)

InitController -> InitController: Store state in session/Redis\nTTL: 5 minutes

InitController -> InitController: Build authorization URL:\nhttps://oauth.vk.com/authorize?\n  response_type=code&\n  client_id={VK_CLIENT_ID}&\n  redirect_uri={CALLBACK_URL}&\n  state={state}&\n  scope=email&\n  display=page&\n  v=5.131

InitController --> User: 302 Found\nLocation: https://oauth.vk.com/authorize?...

deactivate InitController

User -> VKOAuth: User redirected to VK ID
activate VKOAuth

VKOAuth -> VKOAuth: User authenticates\n- Enter VK credentials\n- Or use existing session

VKOAuth -> VKOAuth: User grants permissions:\n- Access to email address

VKOAuth --> User: 302 Found\nLocation: {CALLBACK_URL}?code={AUTH_CODE}&state={state}

deactivate VKOAuth

== OAuth Callback Flow ==

User -> CallbackController: GET /api/v1/auth/oauth/callback?\n  code={AUTH_CODE}&\n  state={state}&\n  provider=vk

activate CallbackController

CallbackController -> CallbackController: Validate CSRF state token\nCompare with stored value

alt Invalid or Expired State Token
  CallbackController --> User: 400 Bad Request\n{\n  "type": "https://cookie.com/errors/oauth-error",\n  "title": "OAuth State Validation Failed",\n  "status": 400,\n  "detail": "Invalid or expired state token (CSRF protection)"\n}
  deactivate CallbackController
end

CallbackController -> VKOAuth: POST https://oauth.vk.com/access_token\nContent-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded\n\ngrant_type=authorization_code&\ncode={AUTH_CODE}&\nclient_id={VK_CLIENT_ID}&\nclient_secret={VK_CLIENT_SECRET}&\nredirect_uri={CALLBACK_URL}

activate VKOAuth

alt Invalid Authorization Code
  VKOAuth --> CallbackController: 400 Bad Request\n{"error": "invalid_grant"}

  CallbackController --> User: 400 Bad Request\n{\n  "type": "https://cookie.com/errors/oauth-error",\n  "title": "OAuth Token Exchange Failed",\n  "status": 400,\n  "detail": "Invalid authorization code"\n}
  deactivate VKOAuth
  deactivate CallbackController
end

VKOAuth --> CallbackController: 200 OK\n{\n  "access_token": "vk1.a.abc123...",\n  "token_type": "Bearer",\n  "expires_in": 86400,\n  "user_id": 12345678,\n  "email": "ivan.petrov@vk.com"\n}

deactivate VKOAuth

CallbackController -> VKOAuth: GET https://api.vk.com/method/users.get?\n  user_ids={user_id}&\n  fields=photo_max,first_name,last_name&\n  access_token={access_token}&\n  v=5.131

activate VKOAuth

VKOAuth --> CallbackController: 200 OK\n{\n  "response": [{\n    "id": 12345678,\n    "first_name": "Ivan",\n    "last_name": "Petrov",\n    "photo_max": "https://sun9-40.userapi.com/.../photo.jpg",\n    "can_access_closed": true,\n    "is_closed": false\n  }]\n}

deactivate VKOAuth

CallbackController -> DB: SELECT * FROM users\nWHERE email = 'ivan.petrov@vk.com'\nOR oauth_provider_id = 'vk:12345678'

activate DB

alt User Already Exists (Link OAuth Account)
  DB --> CallbackController: Existing user found

  CallbackController -> DB: UPDATE users\nSET oauth_provider = 'vk',\n    oauth_provider_id = 'vk:12345678',\n    avatar_url = {vk_photo_max}\nWHERE id = ?
  note right: Link VK account\nto existing email user

else New User (Create Account)
  DB --> CallbackController: No user found

  CallbackController -> DB: INSERT INTO users (\n  id, email, first_name, last_name,\n  oauth_provider, oauth_provider_id,\n  avatar_url, role, subscription_tier,\n  is_active, created_at\n) VALUES (\n  UUID(), 'ivan.petrov@vk.com',\n  'Ivan', 'Petrov', 'vk',\n  'vk:12345678', {photo_max},\n  'user', 'free', true, NOW()\n)
  note right: Create new user\nfrom OAuth data\nNo password_hash needed

  DB --> CallbackController: User created
end

deactivate DB

CallbackController -> JWT: generate_tokens(user.id, user.email, user.role)
activate JWT
JWT -> JWT: Generate access token\n- Payload: {sub, email, role}\n- Expiry: 15 minutes
JWT -> JWT: Generate refresh token\n- Payload: {sub, type, jti}\n- Expiry: 30 days
JWT --> CallbackController: {\n  "access_token": "eyJhbGc...",\n  "refresh_token": "eyJhbGc...",\n  "expires_in": 900\n}
deactivate JWT

CallbackController -> DB: UPDATE users\nSET last_login_at = NOW()\nWHERE id = ?

CallbackController -> DB: INSERT INTO audit_log\n(user_id, action, oauth_provider, created_at)\nVALUES (?, 'oauth_login', 'vk', NOW())

CallbackController --> User: 302 Found\nLocation: {FRONTEND_URL}/auth/success\nSet-Cookie: refresh_token=...; HttpOnly; Secure\nSet-Cookie: access_token=...; HttpOnly; Secure

note right: Redirect to frontend\nwith tokens in cookies\nFrontend reads user data\nfrom /api/v1/users/me

deactivate CallbackController

== Yandex ID Flow (Similar) ==

note over User, DB
  **Yandex ID OAuth Flow:**
  - Similar flow with different endpoints
  - See sequence_auth_oauth_yandex.puml for full Yandex flow
  - Authorization: https://oauth.yandex.ru/authorize
  - Token exchange: https://oauth.yandex.ru/token
  - User info: https://login.yandex.ru/info
  - Scopes: login:email login:info
  - Provider ID format: "yandex:{yandex_user_id}"

  **Account Linking:**
  - Match by email → link to existing user
  - New email → create new user
  - Multiple providers per user supported
  - users.oauth_provider can be: 'yandex', 'vk', or NULL (email/password)
end note

== Error Scenarios ==

note over User, DB
  **OAuth Error Cases:**

  **400 Bad Request:**
  - Invalid state token (CSRF protection)
  - Invalid authorization code
  - Missing required parameters

  **401 Unauthorized:**
  - User denied access at OAuth provider
  - OAuth token expired during flow

  **500 Internal Server Error:**
  - Database connection failure
  - OAuth provider API timeout

  **503 Service Unavailable:**
  - Rate limit exceeded (50 req/hour per IP)
  - OAuth provider unavailable
end note

== VK ID Specifics ==

note over User, DB
  **VK API Requirements:**
  - API version: v5.131 (latest stable)
  - Email scope required: scope=email
  - Email provided in token response (not separate call)
  - User info requires users.get method call
  - Fields: photo_max, first_name, last_name
  - Access token format: vk1.a.{token}
  - Token expiry: 24 hours (86400 seconds)

  **VK OAuth Endpoints:**
  - Authorization: https://oauth.vk.com/authorize
  - Token exchange: https://oauth.vk.com/access_token
  - User info: https://api.vk.com/method/users.get

  **Security Considerations:**
  - VK requires display=page for web apps
  - CSRF protection via state token (mandatory)
  - Email may not be available (user privacy settings)
  - Fallback: use VK user_id as unique identifier
  - Store oauth_provider_id = 'vk:{user_id}'

  **Database Schema:**
  - users.oauth_provider: 'vk'
  - users.oauth_provider_id: 'vk:12345678'
  - users.email: may be NULL if user denied email access
  - users.avatar_url: VK photo_max URL

  **Rate Limits:**
  - VK API: 3 requests per second per user token
  - OAuth endpoints: 50 requests per hour per IP
  - Implement retry with exponential backoff

  **Related Diagrams:**
  - api_auth_endpoints.puml (API specs)
  - sequence_auth_oauth_yandex.puml (Yandex OAuth flow)
  - sequence_auth_register.puml (email/password registration)
  - sequence_auth_login.puml (email/password login)
  - error-handling/error_flow_oauth_failure.puml (future)

  **Backend Implementation:**
  - ASP.NET Core 8 OAuth middleware
  - VK NuGet package: VkNet (optional, or use HttpClient)
  - Environment variables: VK_CLIENT_ID, VK_CLIENT_SECRET
  - Callback URL: https://api.cookie.com/api/v1/auth/oauth/callback?provider=vk
end note

@enduml
